course: dictionary
lesson: 8493
title: Sane and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sane is an adjective with two main meanings. It can mean having a healthy mind that thinks in a normal, clear way. It can also mean sensible and reasonable, as in «a sane decision».
explain: Context tells you which meaning is in use. «No sane person would do that» means the idea is crazy, because no clear-thinking, sensible person would try it.
explain: In everyday talk, «Music keeps me sane during exams» means music helps me stay calm and not feel overwhelmed. The noun is sanity, and «not all there» is an everyday phrase meaning not quite sane, or a bit slow in the head.
fact: Sane means having a healthy mind and thinking in a normal, clear way.
fact: Sane also means sensible and reasonable, as in «a sane decision».
fact: «No sane person would do that» means the idea is crazy.
fact: «Music keeps me sane during exams» means music helps me stay calm.
fact: The noun from sane is sanity.
exercise: «No sane person would do that.» What does this mean? | Anyone would be happy to try it | Only the bravest people could do it | It is a very long job | * It would be a crazy idea, and no sensible person would try it
exercise: «Music keeps me sane during exams.» What does keeps me sane mean? | It makes me sing loudly | It makes me sleep all day | * It helps me stay calm
exercise: Which word is the noun from sane? | sand | * sanity | sadness | sanctuary
test: «It was a ___ decision to wait until the storm had passed.» Choose the word that fits. | famished | glum | barely | * sane
test: Nadia says sane means crazy. Is she right? | * No, sane means healthy-minded and sensible, the opposite of crazy | Yes, sane means very loud | No, sane only means happy | Yes, sane means silly and mad
exam: «Not all there» is said about someone. What does it mean? | Very kind and generous | * Not quite sane, or a bit slow in the head | Sitting down on a chair | Fully awake and very alert
